msgid "Entries render **disabled**, and the task enables each one in the same write that carries its grant. An empty ``access_grants`` is not “nobody”: Open WebUI reads it as every administrator, which is wider than the ``mcp`` group. Since ``ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false`` makes the env authoritative again on every start, an enabled-but-ungranted entry would hand access to all administrators before the first provisioning run and after any bare container restart. A disabled entry is not served at all, so the fallback is no access rather than too much."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Entries render **disabled**, and the task enables each one in the same write that carries its grant. An empty `access_grants` is not \"nobody\": Open WebUI reads it as every administrator, which is wider than the `mcp` group. Since `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false` makes the env authoritative again on every start, an enabled-but-ungranted entry would hand access to all administrators before the first provisioning run and after any bare container restart. A disabled entry is not served at all, so the fallback is no access rather than too much."
msgstr "Entrées **handicapés**, et la tâche permet chacun dans la même écriture qui porte sa subvention. Un vide `access_grants` n'est pas \"nobody\": Open WebUI le lit comme tout administrateur, qui est plus large que le `mcp` Groupe. Depuis `ENABLE_PERSISTENT_CONFIG=false` rend l'env faisant autorité à nouveau sur chaque départ, une entrée activée mais non autorisée donnerait accès à tous les administrateurs avant la première mise à disposition et après tout redémarrage de conteneur nu. Une entrée handicapée n'est pas du tout servie, de sorte que le retour n'est pas un accès plutôt que trop."

