# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (`/translate`, `/detect`, …); see [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under [Single sign-on](#single-sign-on) above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. The `administrator` and `guest` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "Le sidecar authent2-proxy admet seulement LibreTranslate administrateur groupe RBAC et listes blanches juste la machine API chemins (`/translate`, `/detect`, ...); voir [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml). Dans l'application, l'autorisation est API-Tier clé seulement et découplé de l'IDP, tel que documenté sous [Signalisation unique](#single-sign-on) ci-dessus. Un visiteur non-admin n'a donc pas de session d'interface utilisateur à conduire, donc [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) déclare `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`. Les `administrator` et `guest` Les personnes courent sans condition."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar oauth2-proxy admits only the LibreTranslate administrator RBAC group and whitelists just the machine API paths (``/translate``, ``/detect``, …); see ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Single sign-on <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run unconditionally."
msgstr "Le sidecar authent2-proxy admet seulement LibreTranslate administrateur groupe RBAC et listes blanches juste la machine API chemins (``/translate``, ``/detect``, ...); voir ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. Inside the app, authorisation is API-key-tier only and decoupled from the IdP, as documented under `Signalisation unique <#single-sign-on>`__ above. A non-admin visitor therefore has no UI session to drive, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` Les personnes courent sans condition."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an ``upstream.env`` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Le sidecar lit son titre en amont d'un ``upstream.env`` fichier plutôt que de l'environnement de composition, parce que le mot de passe de l'application n'existe pas quand la pile est rendue pour la première fois. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through ``svc-ai-mcp-adapter``\\ ’s ``rebuild.yml``: ``compose up`` resolves ``env_file`` tout en créant le conteneur, qu'un redémarrage ne serait pas."

# libretranslate
msgid "The sidecar reads its upstream credential from an `upstream.env` file rather than from the compose environment, because the app password does not exist when the stack is first rendered. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) writes that file after the mint and recreates the sidecar through `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` resolves `env_file` while creating the container, which a restart would not."
msgstr "Le sidecar lit son titre en amont d'un `upstream.env` fichier plutôt que de l'environnement de composition, parce que le mot de passe de l'application n'existe pas quand la pile est rendue pour la première fois. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) écrit ce fichier après la menthe et recrée le sidecar à travers `svc-ai-mcp-adapter`'s `rebuild.yml`: `compose up` résolu `env_file` tout en créant le conteneur, qu'un redémarrage ne serait pas."

